    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 passing; `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization for owner creation, applied consistently across storage, response, and all address comparisons.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.java`: a small utility that trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands street-type abbreviations token-by-token (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`). Returns `\"\"` for null/blank input, and is idempotent so re-normalizing a stored address is a no-op.\n\n**`RequireOwnerFields.java`** (first step in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline): normalizes the address before the required-field check, rejects it as a `400` when blank after normalization, and republishes the normalized value on the request DTO \u2014 so `BuildOwner` maps the canonical form into the entity, which is what gets stored and returned.\n\n**`RequireUniqueHousehold.java`** and **`AssignHousehold.java`**: both address comparisons (household duplicate detection and the shared household-id hash + back-fill) now route both sides through `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)`, so duplicate detection and household grouping use the normalized form.\n\nAll three new acceptance tests pass (whitespace/case normalization, abbreviation expansion, and blank-after-normalization rejection), and the build is green.",
